<title>UK: UK's OFT to take more time over CE/Northern.</title>
<headline>UK's OFT to take more time over CE/Northern.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK Office of Fair Trading said on Wednesday it is take up to a further 15 days to decide whether or not to recommend referring the purchase of regional electricity company Northern Electric by U.S.-based CalEnergy to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission (MMC).  </p>
<p>A decision on the acquisition from the UK's Department of Trade and Industry is therefore expected by December 16.</p>
<p>CalEnergy has bid $1.225 billion for Northern Electric.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
